-# Iteration 001 — Scaffold versus validate for the three packet types (RQ1)
-
-- Angle: for the packet types **phase / review / research**, what `create.sh` actually writes vs what `check-files.sh` (FILE_EXISTS) and `check-template-source.sh` (TEMPLATE_SOURCE) require, by reading only.
-- Evidence: `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/spec-kit-docs.json` (rows `phase` 2122-2160, `review` 2263-2300, `research` 2381-2427, L1 121-150, L2 502-520); `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/create.sh` (writing paths 940-1013, 1104-1621, 1660-1713; helpers 389-464, 513-588, 590-660, 695-780); `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/rules/check-files.sh` (1-106), `check-template-source.sh` (1-105); `runtime/cli/utils/template-structure.js` (57-73, 190-212, 900-950). Census read once (one call): `confirmed-findings.md` — round-1 (35) + round-2 (34) dispositions loaded; all rows below are new vs both corpora.
-- Tool calls: 6 evidence + 4 write = 10/12. Reads only; no validate.sh, no node, no git.
-
-## How each type is (not) scaffolded — the facts the findings rest on
-
-- **phase** (packet-type row: requiredCoreDocs `[spec.md]`, docs.json:2126-2128; no lifecycleRequiredDocs/optionalAddonDocs — 2129-2130): `create.sh --phase` renders the parent from `packet-types/phase-parent.spec.md.tmpl` through the inline-gate renderer (create.sh:1258), substitutes `[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: …]` tokens (1268-1308), writes spec.md (1310), re-anchors its TEMPLATE_SOURCE marker (1311), writes graph-metadata.json (1313) — then description.json **conditionally** (1426-1434) — then children, each: scratch (1447-1448), graph-metadata stub (1449, *before* any copy), the child contract's documents (1452-1463: requiredCore + lifecycle + AC-if-optional + `--with-goal`/`--with-lazy-addons` extras, 444-464), conditional description.json (1466-1475), finalize+marker relocation (1480, only `if [[ -f _child_spec ]]`, 1479), phase-context anchors (1500-1526). The phase flow exits at 1620-1621; the plain/`--subfolder` machinery (1660-1713) never runs for it.
-- **review / research**: `create.sh` offers no creation path at all — `--level` accepts 1/2/3/3+ only (help 277-278; no `--kind`/`--type`); their contract rows (2263-2300, 2381-2427: requiredCoreDocs `[spec.md, review/review-report.md]` / `[spec.md, research/research.md]`) are consumed only if some caller passes those levels to the rules (VALID_LEVELS admits them: template-structure.js:72). Their documents are workflow-owned (documents[]: `review/review-report.md` owner=workflow, template `null`, 101-106; `research/research.md` owner=workflow, 77-82). Verdict: no scaffold, so no untouched-scaffold failure — the seam is *who exercises those rows*, recorded as open question 3, not a finding.
-
-## Findings (3: 1×P1, 2×P2)
-
-### f-iter001-001 [P1] — The phase parent's rule-required description.json hangs on the untracked dist build
-- CLAIM (`check-files.sh:41-48,55,57`): in the phase-parent branch, a missing `$folder/description.json` is unconditional *missing* — severity **error** ("Phase parent: missing N required file(s): description.json").
-- ACTUAL (`create.sh:1426-1434`, children 1466-1475): the parent's description.json is written only when `APPEND_TO_EXISTING_PARENT != true` **and** `$SCRIPT_DIR/../dist/spec-folder/generate-description.js` exists; either miss → one stderr warning ("description.json generation skipped", 1432) and the scaffold still succeeds. The mirrored plain-path block (1690-1698) has the same dependency, but there the rule never demands the file (check-files.sh:82-86 numbered branch — no description.json) — requirement and guarantee diverge in exactly one place: the phase-parent branch.
-- CONSEQUENCE: in this worktree the untouched `--phase` scaffold passes (the dist generator **exists here**: 6,743 B, Sep 7 09:09 — confirmed by read), but dist/ is untracked and charter-stale; in any checkout without that build, every fresh `--phase` parent silently skips the one file its own FILE_EXISTS rule calls an error, and the scaffolder's own comment rates failure "non-fatal" (1420-1421, in-code note "known gap (F10)" — a code note, not a census row).
-- SEVERITY: P1 (wrong-or-unused: the scaffolder's only non-fatal failure mode is the exactly-one artifact the harshest presence rule demands; the failure surfaces later, as a validation error on an untouched scaffold).
-- RECOMMENDATION: fix — write a bash-minimal description.json fallback (the pattern exists 30 lines away: `create_graph_metadata_file`, create.sh:513-588), or make the generator tracked/checked-in so `-f` cannot silentlymiss.
-
-### f-iter001-002 [P2] — The phase-parent spec's provenance marker is indistinguishable from a plain spec.md's
-- CLAIM (`check-template-source.sh:86-92`): the TEMPLATE_SOURCE marker "proves files were created from official templates" — the rule's own remediation example sells the slug as composition-specific ("spec-core + level2-verify + level3-arch + level3-plus-govern | v2.2", line 90).
-- ACTUAL (`packet-types/phase-parent.spec.md.tmpl:28` vs `core/spec.md.tmpl:36`): both stamp literally `<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core | v2.2 -->` — the lean phase-parent spec self-identifies as a plain core spec; nothing downstream distinguishes them (the `[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: …]` substitution passes the marker line untouched, create.sh:1303-1304; `ensure_template_source_near_top` re-anchors but never rewrites the slug, 590-615; `finalize_scaffold_templates` never runs on the phase parent at all — its only call sites are 769/970/1480/1682).
-- CONSEQUENCE: every other sampled template has a 1:1 slug (`acceptance-criteria | v2.2` at addons/acceptance-criteria.md.tmpl:31, `goal | v2.2` :31, `decision-record | v2.2` :31, `impl-summary-core` core/implementation-summary.md.tmpl:79, `plan-core` :42, `tasks-core` :38) — only the phase-parent variant shares its provenance identity with another template, so provenance-proving is weaker exactly where the template diverges most from its base.
-- SEVERITY: P2 (cosmetic: the rule checks presence, not the slug; but the marker's stated purpose — proving *which* official template — is defeated for this packet type).
-- RECOMMENDATION: fix (distinct slug, e.g. `phase-parent-spec`) or document that the slug names the family, not the file — after open question 4 settles what the parity test pins.
-
-### f-iter001-003 [P2] — Phase children ship a graph-metadata stub the plain path's own comment says would "fail validation the moment it exists"
-- CLAIM (`create.sh:1700-1703`): the plain path's in-code justification for its 1704-1708 backfill — "Derive the graph metadata from the documents that were just written, rather than leaving the stub the scaffolder guessed. A scaffold that disagrees with its own deriver fails validation the moment it exists, which teaches an author that the gate is broken before they have written a line."
-- ACTUAL (`create.sh:1449` vs `1456-1463`, and `513-588`): the phase-children loop writes each child's graph-metadata.json **before** any child document exists (1449 precedes the 1452-1463 copies), so the stub's own elif chain (552-558: `-f spec.md && ! -f plan.md …`, `-f decision-record.md`) can never select anything but the 550-551 default `[spec.md, plan.md, tasks.md]` — at child levels 2/3 the just-scaffolded child then also holds implementation-summary.md (lifecycle, 451+428-442) and acceptance-criteria.md (optional-list, 455-457; L2 row 517-518) that the stub's `key_files`/`source_docs` never mention, and no backfill runs anywhere in 1436-1532 (1704-1708 belongs to the plain path; the phase flow exits at 1620). The same write-before-copies ordering exists on the `--subfolder` path (499 inside `create_versioned_subfolder`, copies at 962-969) — noted here because the defect's mechanism is the children's, which is in this angle's scope.
-- CONSEQUENCE: for `--level 2|3 --phase` the scaffold's stub demonstrably disagrees with its own just-written documents — the exact condition the plain path's comment says it eliminates; whether any check enforces the disagreement is native-land (the two rules here only test existence: `check-files.sh:47-48`), so the finding is the inconsistency, not a proven validation failure.
-- SEVERITY: P2 (cosmetic in impact today — the bash rules test presence only — wrong in principle under the file's own stated invariant).
-- RECOMMENDATION: fix — run the 1704-1708-style backfill for phase children (or move the 1449 stub after the 1456-1463 copies); alternatively weaken the 1700-1703 comment to what actually holds.
-
-## What the angle verified as correct (no finding)
-
-1. Rule↔contract agreement on the three types: FILE_EXISTS for a phase parent = `docs("phase")` = requiredCoreDocs+requiredAddonDocs = `[spec.md]` (check-files.sh:41-46 via template-structure.js:190-193; docs.json:2126-2129) + description.json + graph-metadata.json (47-48) — and the untouched in-this-worktree phase parent has all three (1310-1313 + 1426-1433, dist present).
-2. TEMPLATE_SOURCE's phase remap (check-template-source.sh:37-39: `contract_level="phase"` when `is_phase_parent`) matches the phase row's author-scaffoldable set — `getTemplateSourceDocs('phase')` = `[spec.md]` + 6 author-lazy (template-structure.js:201-207 ∩ docs.json:2131-2139), of which an untouched parent presents exactly `spec.md`, carrying the marker (tmpl:28) placed post-frontmatter by 1311.
-3. Numbered-contract superset property: L1 requiredCoreDocs = `[spec, plan, tasks]` + lifecycle `[implementation-summary.md]` (docs.json:125-134) — scaffolded at 444-464 as requiredCore+lifecycle+AC-if-optional+flag extras; FILE_EXISTS(L1) demands only the requiredCore trio until implementation starts (check-files.sh:65-86) → the untouched scaffold is a compliant superset at every numbered level.
-4. Markers: all 8 sampled `.tmpl` sources carry `SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE` (core 36/42/38/79; addons 31/31/31; packet-types/phase-parent 28) — the rule's premise holds for every template the three types' scaffolds consume.
-5. Remediated behaviors intact under this angle's light: the AC-optional-list decision (452-457, round-1 f-iter001-003's fix), the phase row's narrowed 7-doc lazy list incl. goal.md (2131-2139, round-2 f-iter002-001 parity), the lazy/goal membership guards that hard-exit on contract omission (389-426), child-level inheritance (41-52, the 016 fix), and the phase-children's finalize+marker relocation (1480→657).
-
-## Open questions
-
-1. Lines 1164-1186 and 1090-1103 of create.sh unread: what binds `FEATURE_DIR`/`DOC_LEVEL` in phase mode, and does any argument path other than `--phase` deliver `DOC_LEVEL=phase` to the plain flow — i.e. is 1711-1713 (`scaffold_phase_parent_validation_child`, def 695-780, its own 751-767 child creation at Level 1 with placeholder name 698-699) reachable, and is it redundant with the 1436-1532 loop?
-2. Where does the *phase parent's* goal.md come from under `--with-goal --phase`? `WITH_GOAL`'s only consumer is `scaffold_contract_docs` (461-463), called at 757/958/1452/1670 — none of them is the phase-parent path (1240-1314); the help claims "valid at every level and on phase parents" (283-284). Either lines 1164-1240 (unread) or the 1258 renderer call explains it — unresolved here.
-3. Who invokes the two rules with level=review/research (validate.sh's level sniffing is outside this angle's read set), and does the workflow-written `review/review-report.md` (template `null`, docs.json:101-105) carry a TEMPLATE_SOURCE marker — if not, TEMPLATE_SOURCE(review) fails it (check-template-source.sh:40-66 has no report exemption).
-4. Does the version-parity test (census round-1 f-iter007-001's fix) pin the marker *slug* or only the `| vX` — determines whether f-iter001-002's slug fix is test-safe.
-5. Round-2's f-iter009-001 removed `--sharded`; the help still advertises "Creates spec-sections/ with modular documentation" under `--level` (280) — level vs sections mechanism not audited in this angle's files.
