-Use this section when `research_intent=fix_bug`, when planning from a deep-review FAIL/CONDITIONAL verdict, or when any finding touches security, path handling, env precedence, schema boundaries, persistence, public responses, or shared policy.
-
-| Surface | Current Role | Action | Verification |
-|---------|--------------|--------|--------------|
-| `SKILL.md` `RESOURCE_MAP` and prose links | Routes a 28-file subset of the 45-file corpus by intent | update | `grep -c` the routed-path list against the corpus count, confirming the routed count named at `SKILL.md:95` matches |
-| `references/workflows/quick-reference.md` | First-touch command surface, pointed to by `SKILL.md:129` | update (for files better suited to a pointer than a new intent) | manual read confirms the pointer resolves |
-| `leaf-manifest.json`, `leaf-manifest.config.json` | Enumerate every reference and asset leaf (45 today) | update | `generate-leaf-manifest.cjs --check` exits 0 |
-| Deleted reference/asset file bodies | Currently unreachable content | not a consumer of anything, removed | repo-wide grep for the filename returns nothing outside git history |
-
-Required inventories:
-- Same-class producers: `rg -n 'RESOURCE_MAP|references/|assets/' .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/SKILL.md .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/references/workflows/quick-reference.md`.
-- Consumers of changed symbols: `rg -n '<deleted-filename>' . --glob '*.md' --glob '*.json'` before each deletion.
-- Matrix axes: file identity (17 rows) x disposition (route via intent, route via pointer, remove).
-- Algorithm invariant: not applicable - no parser or resolver logic changes, since this is a routing-surface and manifest edit.
